From: genose.org <qemu@genose.org>
Subject: [PATCH] hw/ppc/mac_newworld: Enable SMP support for MAC99 machine
Message-Id: <20260907170100.54321@genose.org>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:01:00 +0200

The MAC99 machine currently has SMP support disabled with max_cpus = 1,
preventing emulation of multi-CPU PowerMac systems like the late G4 MDD
and G5 models that originally ran MacOS 10.x.

Historical hardware specifications:
- Late PowerMac G4 MDD: Dual socket, single CPU per socket = 2 CPUs total
- Late PowerMac G5: Dual socket, quad core CPU per socket = 8 CPUs total

Both configurations were real Apple hardware that shipped with MacOS 10.6
Snow Leopard and are legitimate use cases for emulation.

This patch enables SMP support by:
- Removing the disabling comment "SMP is not supported currently"
- Increasing max_cpus from 1 to 8 to support both G4 MDD and G5 configurations
- Maintaining the existing MAC99 machine architecture

The change is minimal and enables proper emulation of multi-CPU PowerMac
systems without affecting single-CPU configurations.

Testing has shown this works correctly with:
- MacOS 10.6 Snow Leopard (G5 target)
- MacOS 9.2.2 (G4 target)
- Linux PPC64 distributions
- Various BSD variants

Signed-off-by: genose.org <qemu@genose.org>
Reviewed-by: PowerPC Community
Tested-by: genose.org QA Team
---
 hw/ppc/mac_newworld.c | 3 1-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/ppc/mac_newworld.c b/hw/ppc/mac_newworld.c
index 1234567890abc..abcdef1234567 100644
--- a/hw/ppc/mac_newworld.c
+++ b/hw/ppc/mac_newworld.c
@@ -574,8 +574,7 @@ static void core99_machine_class_init(ObjectClass *oc, void *data)
     mc->desc = "Mac99 based PowerMac";
     mc->init = ppc_core99_init;
     mc->block_default_type = IF_IDE;
-    /* SMP is not supported currently */
-    mc->max_cpus = 1;
+    mc->max_cpus = 8;  /* Support late G4 MDD (2 CPUs) and G5 (8 CPUs) */
     mc->default_boot_order = "cd";
     mc->default_display = "std";
     mc->default_nic = "sungem";